# Flutter workflow

For Flutter tasks, read the app-root `.agents/skills/flutter-workflow/SKILL.md`
and `.agents/skills/flutter-workflow/references/REPOSEED.md` before planning or changing code. Follow their mode
selection and load only the Flutter references needed for the task. This rule
does not apply to unrelated backend or other-stack work.

From this installed rule, the entrypoints are the
[workflow skill](../../../SKILL.md) and
[integration contract](../../../references/REPOSEED.md).

On an initialization request, inspect existing app code and recorded decisions:
greenfield runs orientation-first kickoff; brownfield runs evidence-based
adoption; an adopted app resumes its saved workflow. Reuse confirmed answers.
Review, diagnosis, explanation and planning alone remain read-only. Scaffolding
requires the user's implementation authorization and resolved app choices.

The full SOPs, guardrails, checklists, living-document rules and reporting format
remain in `.agents/skills/flutter-workflow/references/`; the skill routes to them without duplicating the pipeline.
